    "created_at": "2015-12-09T19:37:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-09T19:37:01Z",
    "body": "@zcorpan I have a couple of doubts about that behaviour, maybe you can help me solve them.\n\nNormally I use the natural width and height to read the actual size of the image, my questions are:\n- Since the responsive images are subject to the density-corrected dimensions regarding the viewport, is there a way to retrieve the real size of the image?\n  Right now I'm using  the `currentSrc` of the element to create a new `Image` and read the `naturalWidth` from it, but it feels a bit cumbersome.\n- Could you help me understand the purpose of the correction with a use case?\n\nThank you.\n",
